3-5f92-bdb0-6bd466019f54" :question/math-academy-id "q-38703" :question/problem "Given that $A=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}],$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{7}{5} & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)-\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{5} \\\\  & =-1-\\frac{7}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-38703/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38703"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85921/selection/2535b3c800881f6f50e5a0ef7dcba20efa2624b516601c516d2ba728456a3774" :answer/id #uuid "74b3be57-4521-5c3f-a668-534f8fcaeb62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85921/selection/a0557200b376b42a5de11dfe32d45cfc506d3acb8fa90459610d5f6c27255850" :answer/id #uuid "f087360f-5cb3-5bc2-93d0-ccd7abeec2f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85921/selection/f8f12b478d0323f303a6e66b7a5ba6a7f9a8c130ea62fc433a4fcbcf716a57c6" :answer/id #uuid "5be53fa2-e8a0-51c7-8592-b9ab63521c44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :a