oduct of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2)\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =10-24 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-83393/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-83393"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-83390/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "f9997526-49ca-5017-b9bc-9755f38d6254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83390/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "97a1d694-e70d-56ed-b78a-b789f8132c08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83390/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e3b50d2d-2448-5991-a201-2ebd924ef2df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-83390/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "365136d3-a893-5371-9c59-1ec7a6d53123" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:ans