ution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )-8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2}-5A-2 & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{2}-5A-2) & ={A}^{-1}O \\\\ A-5I-2{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =-\\frac{5}{2}I+\\frac{1}{2}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=-\\frac{5}{2},$ $q=\\frac{1}{2}$ and\n\n$$\np+q=-\\frac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40173/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "152243fa-e0a5-551d-92d9-b470789087c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40173"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85929/selection/cb0f13b631940f95ae300409e0a79e4930c4348071972fd0ee6a41ca971bb2b7" :answer/id #uuid "585af983-247e-541c-a8cd-8617a9ffd49f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9I+2A+{A}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85929/selection/8795c34ffd136e6e943bf9f5bff7f240fba3a5d44cb6c6df33a863e2ec85dd90" :answer/id #uuid "368c154c-f801-5c3e-bfc2-3102afebe4d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{58}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85929/selection/b8c68722da980c421ba9e93b95461e060c9ae5938b5d57e3e46a6d4531b1e2d5" :answer/id #uuid "7a0ed08f-af9f-5110-84c6-6368a02b6622" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85929/selection/b108d94157f16150250145bc5fc02f92fd6def0fbea73ca171599419ae0ea93d" :answer/id #uuid "add64616-c9db-5960-bad9-158a2ab4ae8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "49I-12A+{A}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85929/selection/3e6a48622947babbcb449cd10167996f04516faf733153512994a6c81701e7e3" :answer/id #uuid "5f6e2018-a1ae-5db5-a4fb-933dd759cec1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85929/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fc7a7ec0-7db0-5fc6-967d-3f7b1d9e642a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85929/selection/8795c34ffd136e6e943bf9f5bff7f240fba3a5d44cb6c6df33a863e2ec85dd90" :answer-field/choices ["q-85929/selection/cb0f13b631940f95ae300409e0a79e4930c4348071972fd0ee6a41ca971bb2b7" "q-85929/selection/8795c34ffd136e6e943bf9f5bff7f240fba3a5d44cb6c6df33a863e2ec85dd90" "q-85929/selection/b8c68722da980c421ba9e93b95461e060c9ae5938b5d57e3e46a6d4531b1e2d5" "q-85929/selection/b108d94157f16150250145bc5fc02f92fd6def0fbea73ca171599419ae0ea93d" "q-85929/selection/3e6a48622947babbcb449cd10167996f04516faf733153512994a6c81701e7e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85929" :question/id #uuid "ba3fffe7-2f8e-5856-806c-9ddcf2cb6da2" :question/math-academy-id "q-85929" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],$ then ${A}^{-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((5-\\lambda )^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +29) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+12{\\lambda }^{2}-49\\lambda +58 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{A}^{3}+12{A}^{2}-49A+58I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}(-{A}^{3}+12{A}^{2}-49A+58I) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{2}+12A-49I+58{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{58}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-85929/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "152243fa-e0a5-551d-92d9-b470789087c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85929"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-85931/selection/87381eeebcf1e2cb4eb575a7d9fb1ffd67c7eb5c2b1dd68d2e94d221e004de99" :answer/id #uuid "8f867db1-a6f5-5020-867d-9f0aeda37c78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21A-20I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85931/selection/d95907622fd4dc8197180377f0801943b5c4e181b9da6241fcd0aa4bacc44474" :answer/id #uuid "1eb4b441-2dea-5cb5-83b3-21a1ad8bcfaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21A+20I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85931/selection/bbb221d3d66e6b2eb5ff560118098ba06a75c1eb2465cd61f491e83ba765dbb0" :answer/id #uuid "81c7bace-cf4a-5350-83ed-c27e6841cbbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-21A+20I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85931/selection/216ec2ab53c224a2c84d0bccaf72ffcc4c786be287d9730a481271bf3154c588" :answer/id #uuid "f8f7e3c5-0846-5f35-879e-4681639df46e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-20A-21I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85931/selection/ddca2a710361df38c874acd30d61766c150d65dce0b24fa2868c7297122df073" :answer/id #uuid "758f02ed-0adc-542a-88d6-11185dbbad8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20A+21I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-85931/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c0deb7fd-7d95-5792-a182-81d13a7b3ce4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-85931/selection/d95907622fd4dc8197180377f0801943b5c4e181b9da6241fcd0aa4bacc44474" :answer-field/choices ["q-85931/selection/87381eeebcf1e2cb4eb575a7d9fb1ffd67c7eb5c2b1dd68d2e94d221e004de99" "q-85931/selection/d95907622fd4dc8197180377f0801943b5c4e181b9da6241fcd0aa4bacc44474" "q-85931/selection/bbb221d3d66e6b2eb5ff560118098ba06a75c1eb2465cd61f491e83ba765dbb0" "q-85931/selection/216ec2ab53c224a2c84d0bccaf72ffcc4c786be287d9730a481271bf3154c588" "q-85931/selection/ddca2a710361df38c874acd30d61766c150d65dce0b24fa2868c7297122df073"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-85931" :question/id #uuid "629a4e6c-f5bf-5ddb-918c-4df8c28eff1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-85931" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ then ${A}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{3}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,x$ | $+$ | $1$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-x-20\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{3}\\,\\,}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | $-$ | ${x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $20x$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | ${x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $20x$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | ${x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $x$ | $-$ | $20$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $21x$ | $+$ | $20$ |  |  |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{3}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =q(x)p(x)+(21x+20),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)=x+1.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{3}=q(A)p(A)+(21A+20I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =q(A)p(A)+(21A+20I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(21A+20I) \\\\  & =21A+20I.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-85931/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "787173e1-f957-5ff0-9d14-a6ccb11de1d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-85931"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-38727/selection/7cf973417554f4277cba19ec9c40a1f156ab1328531402da2b2cb1670d3de2c1" :answer/id #uuid "efdf39f1-f416-55ad-b716-51859093a27e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 40 & -22\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38727/selection/dafbc6d8aee7f82f90564b102e347207ff99c53e6a04a45831941b034f8cf765" :answer/id #uuid "bdafffea-1fd3-5a79-b473-7e775e8199a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-20 & 40 \\\\ 0 & 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38727/selection/668185eae7dbba38ff55ad5ffab2ed9bbe19ec279285a1ce1da7a33bca256798" :answer/id #uuid "0eae06e8-3875-55e3-9464-04b45cfa385b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-20 & 22 \\\\ -42 & 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38727/selection/e0c9c176dc26c1bfb92247a63b90444830ac8be2f1e3fd4e99f3fda899f83ab6" :answer/id #uuid "ca60aeea-7d81-5a84-98a9-db0848834037" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38727/selection/1f5479aeeb0649207a797a0c53e39421f33f9a56410b77b51a475ec8f4c440a7" :answer/id #uuid "e4e73cb5-bc0b-5389-b003-a61a4c7b183b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 & 40 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38727/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a39fb50b-962b-52ba-9b84-9510fca09033" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38727/selection/e0c9c176dc26c1bfb92247a63b90444830ac8be2f1e3fd4e99f3fda899f83ab6" :answer-field/choices ["q-38727/selection/7cf973417554f4277cba19ec9c40a1f156ab1328531402da2b2cb1670d3de2c1" "q-38727/selection/dafbc6d8aee7f82f90564b102e347207ff99c53e6a04a45831941b034f8cf765" "q-38727/selection/668185eae7dbba38ff55ad5ffab2ed9bbe19ec279285a1ce1da7a33bca256798" "q-38727/selection/e0c9c176dc26c1bfb92247a63b90444830ac8be2f1e3fd4e99f3fda899f83ab6" "q-38727/selection/1f5479aeeb0649207a797a0c53e39421f33f9a56410b77b51a475ec8f4c440a7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38727" :question/id #uuid "6884fbdf-c141-559a-9c69-73ca1eb1083a" :question/math-academy-id "q-38727" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}]$\nand $f(x)={x}^{23}-25{x}^{21}-4x+2$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda ) \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{21}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-25\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{23}\\,-\\,25{x}^{21}\\,-\\,4x\\,+\\,2}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{23}$ | $-$ | $25{x}^{21}$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  | $-$ | $4x$ | $+$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(-4x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{21}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(-4A+2I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(-4A+2I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-4A+2I) \\\\  & =-4A+2I \\\\  & =-4[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-20 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 20\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-38727/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "787173e1-f957-5ff0-9d14-a6ccb11de1d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38727"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-